Subject: [PATCH 06855/11362] [outer-loop] ARC s5i5 round-3: L3->L4, cracks the
 eight-grow shelf cap

Round-3 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on s5i5 solved L4: rejected round-2's
"all shelves rise above the marker" assumption and instead retracted the
long inner-left shelf DOWNWARD seven bands while still narrow, passing
beside the marker before it widens (parked at rows 45-47, stays below the
marker bar, later growth clips harmlessly against the fixed UI). This
removes the apparent eight-grow hard cap round 2 hit: cascade only the
other three shelves upward and all eleven marker grows reach the diamond.

Independently verified: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver
priority branch (results/outer_loop_codex_s5i5_probe.json, dict-normalized
labels), all 5 trials confirmed level=4, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

L5 explored but not won: couples same-color actuators at different board
locations (E/9 and C/9 couplings); no line found before the click budget
became limiting. Frontier stays at level 4.

reproducible_total_levels 144 -> 145. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

